ate\",\"outputs\":[{\"internalType\":\"address\",\"name\":\"owner\",\"type\":\"address\"}],\"stateMutability\":\"view\",\"type\":\"function\"}],\"devdoc\":{\"kind\":\"dev\",\"methods\":{},\"version\":1},\"userdoc\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"methods\":{},\"notice\":\"Public liquidity recovery is a fee-paying share-owner operation, not an allocator permission. Api3 and Purinta's whole-vault share price can exceed their configured exit-market position (Blue Panic(0x11)); another registered market can release existing assets into vault idle balance. See the detailed case study in tradeexecutor/strategy/vault_protocol/morpho.py and research PR https://github.com/tradingstrategy-ai/vault-notebooks/pull/25. Keep this external library outside the almost-full Safe module bytecode. DELEGATECALL stores only owner-authorised per-vault rate caps in an isolated guard storage slot. A return value makes an unlinked zero library fail closed. The cap is per call, not cumulative: a compromised asset-manager key can repeat a permitted fee-paying operation. This is not a loss-budget policy. Revoking the call site disables execution but retains its configured cap; governance should reconfigure the cap before deliberately re-enabling it.\",\"version\":1}},\"settings\":{\"compilationTarget\":{\"src/lib/MorphoLib.sol\":\"MorphoLib\"},\"evmVersion\":\"cancun\",\"libraries\":{},\"metadata\":{\"bytecodeHash\":\"none\"},\"optimizer\":{\"enabled\":true,\"runs\":1},\"remappings\":[\"/home/mikko/code/trade-executor-worktrees/vault-of-vaults-round-3/deps/web3-ethereum-defi/contracts/guard/lib/forge-std/:ds-test/=lib/forge-std/lib/ds-test/src/\",\"/home/mikko/code/trade-executor-worktrees/vault-of-vaults-round-3/deps/web3-ethereum-defi/contracts/guard/lib/hyper-evm-lib/:forge-std/=lib/hyper-evm-lib/lib/forge-std/src/\",\"/home/mikko/code/trade-executor-worktrees/vault-of-vaults-round-3/deps/web3-ethereum-defi/contracts/guard/lib/hyper-evm-lib/:openzeppelin-contracts/=lib/hyper-evm-lib/lib/openzeppelin-co